{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets","id":606155,"title":"Angellic equivalents to Gadgets?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-28T18:45:47-07:00","id":606155,"title":"Angellic equivalents to Gadgets?","content":"I was wondering, have any of you found reason to equip hunter angels with gear or weaponry that is analogous to Gadgets? I ask because I am quite curious to see what sort of advantages most storytellers give their angellic antagonists, because I fel like I may make my angels a little too well equip for my players to handle ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T20:28:17-07:00","id":606285,"title":"","content":"I thought about it. But then I couldn't la merit a reason as to why. Since angels are designed for a specific purpose and get the info from the God-machine they need to assist them. It didn't make much sense on my end. If the angel couldn't do the job as is, it would be replaced with a better model right?<br /> <br /> Though I'm toying with with an idea of artifact items made from scraps/ corpses of angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T20:47:15-07:00","id":606306,"title":"","content":"I suspect Angels don't need Gadgets. They have certain other advantages to make them frighteningly powerful. Having admin access to the universe is quite useful!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T21:46:20-07:00","id":606325,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh... Sort of. I just made an angel based off of Fi from Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword, and she's Fettered to a relic sword. Granted, she's just there to provide assistance to &quot;Fate's chosen Hero&quot; (which in this case means somebody with Resolve 5), so that doesn't really count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T21:54:41-07:00","id":606329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets#post606155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, ... I feel like I may make my angels a little too well equipped for my players to handle ^^;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the fluff, I think that's <i>exactly</i> how angels are supposed to roll out against Unchained.<br /> <br /> The Loyalist have all the advantages: they're backed by the effectively unlimited power of the G-M, they have full access to the levers and knobs of reality, they're in the system. Gadgets are really only useful for demons, since they need to scrap together any advantage they can.<br /> <br /> The closest analogue I can see to what an angel might use for a gadget are the tattoos of the Knights of St. Adrian, which empower an angel's pawns/dupes/cultists, but the angels themselves can bend, fold, staple and mutilate reality however they want. There's not really much call a magic sword or other tool, the G-m gives them what they need to accomplish their mission parameters.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T22:19:48-07:00","id":606340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets?p=606329#post606329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest analogue I can see to what an angel might use for a gadget are the tattoos of the Knights of St. Adrian, which empower an angel's pawns/dupes/cultists, but the angels themselves can bend, fold, staple and mutilate reality however they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Well. However &quot;They&quot; want, really, if we're being technical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's not really much call a magic sword or other tool, the G-m gives them what they need to accomplish their mission parameters. </div> </div> </div>There is, of course, the prospect of The Plan calling for the handing off and demonstration of said relics, but given the general tenor of the Machine's practices it's more likely that such a tool would itself be an angel to better moderate the use of supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T23:52:21-07:00","id":606397,"title":"","content":"The angelic equivalent to gadgetry is infrastructure.<br /> <br /> If an angel needs the help, the G-M would send it the angel's way or have the angel build it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T01:47:24-07:00","id":606429,"title":"","content":"The Quickstart contains an Angelic &quot;Gadget&quot; in the form of a coin with angelic script around the edges, which functions as a tracking device for an Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T05:08:07-07:00","id":606480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets?p=606397#post606397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The angelic equivalent to gadgetry is infrastructure.<br /> <br /> If an angel needs the help, the G-M would send it the angel's way or have the angel build it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Infrastructure is really an overused term in DtD, it can mean a lot - from cultists to magic items, to certain places and even certain times. But, yes, StSword is basically right. I remember reading in one of the books about a kind of Infrastructure that made a stamp that, when used on a book, would make all copies of that book vanish from the world, or something similar. There's descriptions of magic wood that blocks aetheric signals as part of the G-M infrastructure. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T20:11:23-07:00","id":607443,"title":"","content":"While angels have a much greater control of reality than demons (well as much as their &quot;father&quot; allows) and Infrastructure definitely provides much, Perhaps I should of asked whether or not do the various storytellers equip their angels with tools and weapons that could be likened to Gadgets in terms of being supernatural equipment that is tailor made for their angellic users ( like the essence swords in the opening fiction for the core book)- either produced by Infrastructure or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T20:31:01-07:00","id":607457,"title":"","content":"That kind of thing would just function as an aspect of the Angel's own abilities, at least in my games. For flavour purposes, yeah, the angel might be wielding a flaming sword of essence, but in game mechanics it would just be a way of stating how its Numen/Influence/other abilities work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T20:49:46-07:00","id":607463,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T23:14:36-07:00","id":607522,"title":"","content":"What Azahul said. An Angel might be using the Blast Numina like any other spirit (boosted by so called admin access to reality) but it will appear as though the 'Man in Black' is firing a big-ass gun that tears cars apart. Or never running out of ammo. Or from 3 blocks away. Or all combined.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Demons are a paranoid bunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T23:19:42-07:00","id":607528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets?p=607522#post607522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Azahul said. An Angel might be using the Blast Numina like any other spirit (boosted by so called admin access to reality) but it will appear as though the 'Man in Black' is firing a big-ass gun that tears cars apart. Or never running out of ammo. Or from 3 blocks away. Or all combined.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Demons are a paranoid bunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It also bears mentioning that, yes, the quickstart has an angelic tracking device, but the quickstart also has its angel modeled using non-ephemeral rules for the sake of space and ephemeral beings have the innate ability to track nearby instances of suitably tagged Influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:06:27-07:00","id":607959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets?p=607443#post607443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While angels have a much greater control of reality than demons (well as much as their &quot;father&quot; allows) and Infrastructure definitely provides much, Perhaps I should of asked whether or not do the various storytellers equip their angels with tools and weapons that could be likened to Gadgets in terms of being supernatural equipment that is tailor made for their angellic users ( like the essence swords in the opening fiction for the core book)- either produced by Infrastructure or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.... Okay.<br /> <br /> I've made up a few special merits for Angels to have, mostly centered around making Angels more espionage/surveillance themed: subverted organizations/institutions, networks of sleeper agents, etc. I give Angels form powers, and I've plundered the Vampyramid mechanic from Nights Black Agents and the Antagonist Reactions from Esoterrorist: each angel my player deal with has a unique set of escalating responses that get nastier until the players back off (or die)<br /> <br /> I think the best thing you can do, at least until the STG hits, is get creative with what an angel can do with their Influences. For example, when my player ran into Grief (GMC 136). He's a rank 1 angel, and a few of my more combat focused players were unimpressed. Grief just said, &quot;Did you think there was only one Key?&quot; Cue the room suddenly having dozens of serial killers from throughout history in the room with them. <br /> <br /> Jenn (GMC 136) during a negotiation with the players, when one of them made a threat she smiled and said, &quot;hun, look at your wallet, no, your <i>other wallet</i>&quot; and the players say a picture of Jenn as the nurse in the delivery room where the Guardian/Tempter's first child was born.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:15:43-07:00","id":608132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/606155-angellic-equivalents-to-gadgets?p=607522#post607522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Azahul said. An Angel might be using the Blast Numina like any other spirit (boosted by so called admin access to reality) but it will appear as though the 'Man in Black' is firing a big-ass gun that tears cars apart. Or never running out of ammo. Or from 3 blocks away. Or all combined.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Demons are a paranoid bunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Well, don't forget that demons and angels are both robots. Their flaming swords are often times built into their own bodies. If the God Machine wants to give an angel the &quot;Sword of St Michael&quot; or something, it'd be installed directly into their body. Most &quot;angelic gadgets&quot; will likely be something used by cultists directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:24:29-07:00","id":608595,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine could certainly build/summon Angel X and tell it to use its Claim Manifestation on an object (that is, making it a pseudo Gadget) and wait until Angel Y/Cult Z comes to get it. But what circumstances could make it crucial to send two Angels on a mission that can be accomplished with one? Can such circumstances be avoided preemptively? And wouldn't that pseudo Gadget produce significant Essence trails that can be tracked by the right Demons?<br /> <br /> &quot;My agents have no need for redundant, leaky equipment. Any rogue element that thinks I would make a plan so basic as to be derailed by a missing object is the kind of rogue that doesn't know it is still helping me.&quot;<br /> <br /> - God-Machine, maybe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-31-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}